  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds stack write when a bz2 decompressor or\n     BZ2File handle is reused after a decompression error\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-9669.patch: record the bzlib error code on\n       BZ2DecompObject and refuse further decompress() calls with\n       ValueError in Modules/bz2module.c, so that crafted input can no\n       longer make BZ2_bzDecompress() resume from an invalid internal\n       state; also make the error sticky for the C BZ2File read paths,\n       which re-entered the errored stream in the same way, and add\n       regression tests for both\n     - CVE-2026-9669",
